{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01004",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 5.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.38,
      "end_seconds": 10.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.91,
      "end_seconds": 17.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.51,
      "end_seconds": 22.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.49,
      "end_seconds": 38.66,
      "duration_seconds": 14.17,
      "text": "Doctor, it's a tight feeling in my chest when I walk uphill. It's getting on my nerves now. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.3,
      "end_seconds": 40.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Does anything help it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.13,
      "end_seconds": 45.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "It settles a little with stopping and resting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.93,
      "end_seconds": 49.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.21,
      "end_seconds": 55.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Maybe a four out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.69,
      "end_seconds": 63.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Alright, any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.51,
      "end_seconds": 73.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "Erm, when it starts I tend to get a heaviness in my left arm as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.67,
      "end_seconds": 75.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Have you been feeling tired?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.7,
      "end_seconds": 83.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Yes, actually. With heaviness in my left arm, mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.54,
      "end_seconds": 89.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Did you get ankle swelling, pain between the shoulder blades or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.42,
      "end_seconds": 94.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.87,
      "end_seconds": 97.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Right, right. How about palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.13,
      "end_seconds": 100.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "No, um, no palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 101.49,
      "end_seconds": 106.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice palpitations. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.23,
      "end_seconds": 114.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.85,
      "end_seconds": 123.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.24,
      "end_seconds": 126.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.62,
      "end_seconds": 130.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.26,
      "end_seconds": 132.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.43,
      "end_seconds": 136.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.9,
      "end_seconds": 143.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster tramadol gave me feeling very drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.05,
      "end_seconds": 156.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.0,
      "end_seconds": 165.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "Yes, I had a cataract operation in my left eye, about a year ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.67,
      "end_seconds": 170.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.09,
      "end_seconds": 174.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 175.91,
      "end_seconds": 185.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, she is supposed to take it every morning, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.52,
      "end_seconds": 191.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "I'm on gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.52,
      "end_seconds": 209.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.93,
      "end_seconds": 228.38,
      "duration_seconds": 16.45,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about a year. Diabetes, for nearly five years. I did try to ignore it for a while. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.74,
      "end_seconds": 242.08,
      "duration_seconds": 12.34,
      "text": "Right, right. Right, yes, high blood pressure is known to us, good to have that clear. What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.47,
      "end_seconds": 247.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.31,
      "end_seconds": 252.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.73,
      "end_seconds": 256.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 264.46,
      "end_seconds": 273.11,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Temp 36.8 degrees, BP is 118 over 75. Heart rate 84, saturation 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.09,
      "end_seconds": 275.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.15,
      "end_seconds": 280.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.54,
      "end_seconds": 283.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.55,
      "end_seconds": 296.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmur, and the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.09,
      "end_seconds": 300.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.51,
      "end_seconds": 311.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "There is no swelling in your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.08,
      "end_seconds": 325.54,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Putting it all together, the most likely explanation is exertional angina until proven otherwise. I'd also keep a muscle strain in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.65,
      "end_seconds": 328.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.35,
      "end_seconds": 349.0,
      "duration_seconds": 19.65,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's exertional angina until proven otherwise, and we'll know more once the an ECG is back. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had a tight feeling in your chest when you walk uphill, and no cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.92,
      "end_seconds": 354.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 355.53,
      "end_seconds": 359.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I've already done an ECG, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.92,
      "end_seconds": 365.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Right, thank you. Any scans or blood work done already?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.67,
      "end_seconds": 375.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "I had blood tests done at another clinic last year. I don't have the report with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.76,
      "end_seconds": 402.91,
      "duration_seconds": 25.15,
      "text": "I think an exercise stress test makes sense here, for exertional chest tightness. I'm going to put you on aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day, long term. That should help with heart protection. We'll begin with GTN spray, 400 micrograms, when needed for chest pain, long term. It's for chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.54,
      "end_seconds": 406.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "How soon will it work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.23,
      "end_seconds": 429.94,
      "duration_seconds": 18.71,
      "text": "If the tightness comes, stop, sit down and use the spray under your tongue. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. I'm going to send a referral to the cardiology clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 431.51,
      "end_seconds": 434.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.58,
      "end_seconds": 444.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "Let's review you after the test results are back. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.93,
      "end_seconds": 448.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.74,
      "end_seconds": 451.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Okay, take care now."
    }
  ]
}